  "note": "Poll on Wednesday 18 May 1955; 75 per cent polled. Five candidates for four seats in the North-West (Navan Street) ward. George M'Kenna, elected in 1952 for the Eire Labour Party, stood as an Independent. Retiring members: M'Kenna, Cauldwell, Mrs Agnew and Trainor; Felix Hughes returned to the council."
